          },
          "mechanism": "Weight is associated with metabolic status and insulin requirement (dosing is weight-dependent). Heavier individuals have higher baseline insulin needs and may have metabolic syndrome affecting liver health.",
          "justification": "Could confound if weight affects both insulin dose and liver disease risk. However, this is current weight (not weight at disease onset), and the temporal relationship to outcome (age at cirrhosis diagnosis) is unclear. Weight may be a mediator (metabolic status → insulin dose) rather than a confounder.",
